As a side note to this little adventure, the character ascended
today...thanks to a pair of fairly well-equipped bones, my gem count was
really high (at least for me)...I also hoarded amulets a bit. There would
be more, but I decided I wanted intrinsic magical breathing, so I ate about
4 or 5 of those as a Xorn.

Nearly died in Air, I forgot to bring a conflict ring with me, and got
stunned + engulfed by an air elemental. Knocked me down to 50 hp or so
before I woke up to chug a full heal. Then an Archon showed up, and 3 turns
in a row summoned extra monsters. That was ugly...my other ascensions had
been with lawful characters, I'd never faced a hostile Archon before.

 Easiest Astral Plane yet (my third), not because of being a wizard,
although expert Cone of Cold and Fireball were nice, but because the Riders
were imbeciles. Had to visit all 3 wings to find my altar, but Famine was
out visiting relatives the whole time, and he never came out from behind
the temple building. Pestilence I had to wipe out 6 times or so, but Death
came over after I had wiped out the Pestilence wing...I maneuvered Death so
that my guardian angel was opposite, and then bounced magic missiles off of
our reflection until Death was...dead. Then we walked over to his wing, and
he never came back from the Pestilence side. I even had time to burn a few
wishes (this game was nuts for /oW...I found 4) to make a cursed created
monster summon and a blessed taming scroll.

